# Markerless-seeker prototype (ADR-0033 item 2): isolated venv, downloaded model
# weights, and regenerable eval artifacts — the .py modules ARE tracked.
.venv-seeker/
scripts/seeker/weights/
scripts/seeker/out/
scripts/seeker/eval_out/
scripts/seeker/twostage_out/
scripts/seeker/eval_tag_boxes.json

# Drone-specific detector lane (ADR-0033 task #9): its own train/export venv
# (torch/ultralytics, large) and downloaded/generated training data — the
# drone_detector_eval.py / train_drone_finetune.py modules ARE tracked.
.venv-seeker-train/
scripts/seeker/data/

# Bench/field CAPTURE SESSIONS written by scripts/seeker/pi_capture.py --out.
# The frames are bulky and regenerable by re-running the capture; the tiny
# per-session aggregates are NOT (they carry applied exposure, the two measured
# rates, and the tag rows a scorer joins against), so they are re-included and
# committed under runs/ the same way logs/*.csv gate evidence is above.
# WHY THIS RULE EXISTS (2026-08-10): sessions/ was untracked-and-unignored, so
# the skr-05 session sat on one microSD card while project_state.json quoted its
# numbers, and the next capture would have shown up as untracked noise -- or been
# swept into a commit whole, frames and all.
sessions/*/frames/
sessions/**/*.png

# Gazebo / PX4 caches that can leak into the workspace
.gz/
build/

# Demo-video capture output (regenerable frame sequences + large MP4/GIF;
# demo_out/README.md explains the pipeline and IS tracked despite the
# directory-wide ignore below. A couple of committed sample stills live in
# docs/images/ instead of here.
demo_out/*
!demo_out/README.md
# The RETIREMENT NOTE is tracked even though the media it describes is not
# (ADR-0094, 2026-08-10). The assets were retired for making a ram-kill claim
# the project cannot support; the REASON has to outlive the local copy of the
# files, or a future session finds five orphaned videos and no explanation and
# is one step from republishing them.
# NOTE the three-line dance: git cannot re-include a path inside a fully ignored
# DIRECTORY, so the directory is un-ignored, its CONTENTS re-ignored, and then
# only the README un-ignored again. Un-ignoring the directory alone would commit
# the five retired video files themselves (~8 MB) — verified with git check-ignore.
!demo_out/retired_2026-08-10/
demo_out/retired_2026-08-10/*
!demo_out/retired_2026-08-10/README.md

